note TWIN of ce-view.om with every unroll and inline removed (section 4 lines 91, 97): OM-2 unit,
note same expectations per selector.
note Contract section 4 lines 105-108 and section 6 line 170, errata E2: every index into an UNSIZED view
note keeps its run-time check (trap 3), also when it is a constant after unrolling or inlining. b holds
note 1 10 100 ... 10^7; the callee sees a part of b (or the 4-element a4 = b[0..4), E2) and reads one
note element past its length, which in b is a defined neighbour: a compiler that drops the check prints
note it and exits 0 instead of trapping. One stdin byte selects:
note   A sumv part b 0 4 (unrolled 5 reads): 1 11 111 1111, trap 3          exit 103
note   B sumv a4 (sized array to view ulong *, E2): 1 11 111 1111, trap 3   exit 103
note   C sumi part b 0 4 (sumv inlined): 1 11 111 1111, trap 3               exit 103
note   D getc part b 0 4 (constant get v 6, no unroll): trap 3               exit 103
note   E sumv part b 0 5 (in range): 1 11 111 1111 11111, then 11111         exit 0
note   F sumv part b 3 4: 1000 11000 111000 1111000, trap 3                  exit 103
note Twin ce-view-plain.om (unroll and inline removed) has the same expectations; OM-1 approximation
note ce-view-om1.om uses sized views. Expected: oracle/s3s4/exp/ce-view-*.out (python3).
om2
fn sumv v view ulong * to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 5
s = add s get v i
pu s
end
ret s
end
fn sumi v view ulong * to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 5
s = add s get v i
pu s
end
ret s
end
fn getc v view ulong * to ulong
ret get v 6
end
fn main to int
sb = new uchar 1 0
r = read 0 sb 0 1
k = get sb 0
b = new ulong 8 0
a4 = new ulong 4 0
p = ulong 1
for j ulong 8
put b j p
p = mul p 10
end
for j ulong 4
put a4 j get b j
end
if eq k 65
pu sumv part b 0 4
end
if eq k 66
pu sumv a4
end
if eq k 67
pu sumi part b 0 4
end
if eq k 68
pu getc part b 0 4
end
if eq k 69
pu sumv part b 0 5
end
if eq k 70
pu sumv part b 3 4
end
ret 0
end
